<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fu Jiezi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 65 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fu Jiezi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> envoy to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-regions">Western Regions</a> in the reign of Emperor Zhao. In 77 BCE he assassinated the king of Loulan, who had sided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>, after which the Han installed a new king and renamed the kingdom Shanshan. The deed made him a model of bold service abroad in later Chinese tradition.</p></div>
